% sale-contract.l4
%
% The Logical English (for LPS) twin of the contracts of an L4 file (sale-contract.l4), written
% by the L4 translator (docs/migration/l4.md, step 3). Each obligation, permission or
% prohibition is a fluent that holds while it is open; the events are L4's, with the day
% L4 gives them as their last place. As L4's evaluator does, a missed deadline is
% noticed when something next happens, and that event does not count towards what
% follows. Each #TRACE of the file is a scenario; the comment above it is L4's result.
%
% DISCLAIMER. This program was written by a translator from a program of another
% system. It is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind, express or
% implied, including any warranty that it is accurate, complete or fit for a
% particular purpose. The translation may be wrong: check it against its source
% before relying on it. It is not legal, tax, insurance, financial or other
% professional advice. Its authors accept no liability for any loss or damage
% arising from its use.

the target language is: lps.

the maximum time is 4.

the events are:
    the contract the sale contract starts on day *a day*; known as contract_the_sale_contract_starts.
    *a party* does deliver the goods on day *a day*; known as does_deliver_the_goods.
    something happens on day *a day*; known as something_happens_on_day.
    *a party* does something on day *a day*; known as does_something_on_day.
    the clock reaches day *a day*; known as the_clock_reaches_day.
    *a party* does pay the invoice on day *a day*; known as does_pay_the_invoice.
    *a party* does cancel the order on day *a day*; known as does_cancel_the_order.

the fluents are:
    the sale contract obliges *a party* to deliver the goods by day *a due day* as its first obligation; known as o_the_sale_contract_1.
    the sale contract obliges *a party* to pay the invoice by day *a due day* as its second obligation; known as o_the_sale_contract_2.
    the sale contract permits *a party* to cancel the order as its third obligation; known as o_the_sale_contract_3.
    the contract is fulfilled; known as the_contract_is_fulfilled.
    the contract is breached; known as the_contract_is_breached.

the knowledge base sale_contract includes:

the text of "the L4 source sale-contract.l4" is at "sources/sale-contract.l4".

something happens on day a day from a time to a second time if
    the clock reaches day the day from the time to the second time.

something happens on day a day from a time to a second time if
    a party does deliver the goods on day the day from the time to the second time.

a party does something on day a day from a time to a second time if
    the party does deliver the goods on day the day from the time to the second time.

something happens on day a day from a time to a second time if
    a party does pay the invoice on day the day from the time to the second time.

a party does something on day a day from a time to a second time if
    the party does pay the invoice on day the day from the time to the second time.

something happens on day a day from a time to a second time if
    a party does cancel the order on day the day from the time to the second time.

a party does something on day a day from a time to a second time if
    the party does cancel the order on day the day from the time to the second time.

% The contract the sale contract starts: its first obligations.
when the contract the sale contract starts on day a day
    and a due day = day + 14
then the sale contract obliges the_seller to deliver the goods by day the due day as its first obligation.

% The first obligation of the sale contract: met, or its deadline missed.
when a party does deliver the goods on day a day
    and the sale contract obliges the party to deliver the goods by day a due day as its first obligation
    and the day <= the due day
    and a second due day = day + 30
then the sale contract obliges the_buyer to pay the invoice by day the second due day as its second obligation
    and it is not the case that the sale contract obliges the party to deliver the goods by day the due day as its first obligation.

when something happens on day a day
    and the sale contract obliges a party to deliver the goods by day a due day as its first obligation
    and the day > the due day
then the sale contract permits the_seller to cancel the order as its third obligation
    and it is not the case that the sale contract obliges the party to deliver the goods by day the due day as its first obligation.

% The second obligation of the sale contract: met, or its deadline missed.
when a party does pay the invoice on day a day
    and the sale contract obliges the party to pay the invoice by day a due day as its second obligation
    and the day <= the due day
then the contract is fulfilled
    and it is not the case that the sale contract obliges the party to pay the invoice by day the due day as its second obligation.

when something happens on day a day
    and the sale contract obliges a party to pay the invoice by day a due day as its second obligation
    and the day > the due day
then the contract is breached
    and it is not the case that the sale contract obliges the party to pay the invoice by day the due day as its second obligation.

% The third obligation of the sale contract: met, or its deadline missed.
when a party does cancel the order on day a day
    and the sale contract permits the party to cancel the order as its third obligation
then the contract is fulfilled
    and it is not the case that the sale contract permits the party to cancel the order as its third obligation.

